    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d147">

                <pb facs="0277" n="111" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/2740</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-28T21:00:00+08:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 28, 1917, 9 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Resignation of General Tuan accepted. Minister of Foreign Affairs designated
                    temporal Premier. Have private information to the effect that General Tuan would
                    like to devote himself to work for assistance to Allies in the war. I believe he
                    could advantageously be intrusted with this matter. His personal honesty and
                    loyalty are generally recognized and his appointment as high commissioner for
                    the above purpose would be widely approved.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reinsch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
